# CENTER (source position for a beam centred at an element + offset), FFP (field for a chief-ray
# target at an element), PFP (the same in pixels), FDP (detector position from the chief rays) on
# the manual's Cassegrain (cmdref: Ray Tracing).  CENTER 3 with a 10 mm offset moves ChfRayPos y
# to 4.03e-2 (RAY 1 shows it); FFP and PFP converge in 2 iterations; FDP updates element 5.
# The chief ray is obscured at the detector (element 1's shadow) and the solvers proceed anyway.
old $ROOT/docs/macos-manual/examples/Cassegrain.in
stop obj 0 0 0
center 3 0.01,0
ray
1
0
ffp 5 1e-3,-2e-3
yes
pfp 5 15e-4 20,-100
yes
fdp 5
yes
# EXPECT: Beam centered in\s+\d+ iterations, error=\s+\d\.\d+D-1\d
# EXPECT: Starting point=\s+\S+\s+4\.03328628\d+D-02\s+-5\.00000000000000D\+00
# EXPECT: Chief ray obscured at element\s+5
# EXPECT: Field angle finder results:\s+Did\s+\d iterations, error=\s+\d\.\d+D-1\d\s+Old dx=\s+\S+\s+New dx=\s+1\.0000000\d\dD-03
# EXPECT: Old dx=\s+1\.0000000\d\dD-03\s+New dx=\s+3\.0000000\d\dD-02
# EXPECT: New Detector Normal   =\s+-4\.41659775810825\d*E-003
# EXPECT: Detector Element Position \( Elt\s+5 \) Updated!
# EXPECT-NOT: forrtl
